 choice('r1','What was the original reason for using examination rankings?',['Reducing favouritism','Reducing living costs','Increasing mentoring attendance'],0,'A says a clear numerical ranking was intended to prevent favouritism.'),tf('r2','The original application requested household income.','FALSE','A says applicants were not asked about household income.'),tf('r3','The external review found that every scholarship winner lacked ability.','FALSE','A explicitly says the review did not conclude that winners lacked ability.'),gap('r4','NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS: New contextual evidence could include ___ responsibilities.','caring','B lists caring responsibilities as contextual evidence.'),tf('r5','Financial need became the only selection criterion.','FALSE','B says academic readiness remained necessary.'),heading('r6','Best heading for paragraph C?',['The costs beyond tuition','A compulsory mentoring scheme','Selecting on examination scores alone'],0,'C explains rent, transport and lost earnings, followed by a living-cost allowance.'),gap('r7','ONE WORD: Mentoring attendance was ___.','voluntary','D explicitly describes attendance as voluntary.'),choice('r8','Why should the mentoring result be interpreted cautiously?',['All meetings were cancelled.','Motivation could influence both attendance and completion.','Completion was not measured.'],1,'D gives motivation as a possible confounding influence.'),tf('r9','The foundation published each recipient’s personal income.','FALSE','E states individual incomes were not published.'),choice('r10','Which funding option did the foundation initially choose?',['More awards with no allowance','Fewer students with fuller support','No scholarships for three years'],1,'E says it chose to support fewer students more fully.'),tf('r11','The revised scheme eliminated every disadvantage.','FALSE','F acknowledges that not every disadvantage could be removed.'),choice('r12','Which tension is central to the passage?',['Administrative simplicity versus responsiveness to circumstances','University rankings versus building design','Online lectures versus classroom teaching'],0,'F contrasts a simple rule with a more responsive rule requiring judgement and resources.')
