 listening:[
 {title:'Part A · Scholarship advice appointment',script:'Your scholarship advice appointment is confirmed for Wednesday at two forty five in the afternoon. We first offered two fifteen, but the adviser has a meeting then. Please go to the admissions centre, room twenty six. Bring your transcript and a draft budget. You do not need a reference letter for this appointment. The application deadline is the third of October, while supporting documents can arrive until the tenth. The award covers tuition and a monthly allowance of six hundred pounds. Travel costs are not included. Advice appointments are free, but you must cancel at least twenty four hours in advance if you cannot attend. The adviser recommends allowing forty minutes for the meeting.',questions:[gap('l1','Write a time: The appointment starts at ___.',['2:45','14:45','2.45','two forty five'],'2:15 is the earlier offer, not the confirmed time.'),gap('l2','ONE NUMBER: The room number is ___.','26','The meeting is in room 26 at the admissions centre.'),choice('l3','Which document is NOT needed for this appointment?',['Transcript','Draft budget','Reference letter'],2,'The speaker explicitly excludes the reference letter.'),gap('l4','Write the application deadline (day and month).',['3 October','October 3','third of October','3rd October'],'October 10 is for supporting documents, not the application.'),gap('l5','ONE NUMBER: The monthly allowance is £___.','600','The stated allowance is £600 per month.'),choice('l6','What is excluded from the award?',['Tuition','Monthly allowance','Travel costs'],2,'The speaker explicitly says travel is not included.')]},
 {title:'Part B · Evaluating student support',script:'Our evaluation followed two hundred scholarship recipients over three years. We found that students using mentoring services completed their degrees more frequently. This is an association, not necessarily evidence that mentoring caused the difference. Students who actively seek support may already be more motivated. We also interviewed students who rejected an award. Rent and lost earnings were mentioned more often than tuition, since tuition was already covered. As a result, the foundation added a living cost allowance. Next year, we plan to collect baseline information before students begin mentoring. We will compare students with similar academic histories, although this cannot account for every difference. Interviews will remain important because completion statistics cannot reveal why a student leaves. Personal financial information will be kept confidential.',questions:[gap('l7','ONE NUMBER: The evaluation followed ___ recipients.','200','The opening says two hundred recipients.'),choice('l8','What can be concluded about mentoring?',['It definitely caused higher completion.','Its use was associated with higher completion.','It had no relationship with completion.'],1,'The speaker explicitly distinguishes association from causation.'),gap('l9','ONE WORD: Students seeking support may be more ___.','motivated','Motivation is the suggested alternative explanation.'),choice('l10','Which costs were often mentioned by students rejecting an award?',['Rent and lost earnings','Books and sports fees','Tuition only'],0,'Rent and lost earnings were mentioned more often than tuition.'),gap('l11','ONE WORD: Next year, researchers will collect ___ information before mentoring begins.','baseline','Baseline information records starting conditions.'),choice('l12','Why are interviews still necessary?',['To publish personal incomes','To understand reasons for leaving','To replace all statistics'],1,'Statistics cannot reveal why a student leaves.')]}
 ],
