 reading:[choice('r1','What distinguishes an adaptive platform?',['It assigns exercises based on previous responses.','It never repeats a question.','It only teaches in classrooms.'],0,'A explains selection based on earlier answers.'),tf('r2','Every incorrect response proves a learner misunderstands a concept.','FALSE','A gives misreading and accidental button presses as alternatives.'),gap('r3','ONE NUMBER: The trial lasted ___ weeks.','12','B describes a twelve-week trial.'),tf('r4','Participants were randomly allocated to the platform group.','FALSE','B says they volunteered and were not randomly assigned.'),choice('r5','Why is volunteering a limitation?',['Volunteers may already be more motivated.','Volunteers cannot learn vocabulary.','No comparison group existed.'],0,'B notes enthusiasm about independent study as a potential difference.'),heading('r6','Best heading for paragraph C?',['When slower practice produces better retention','The elimination of delayed testing','A new privacy rule'],0,'C contrasts slower practice with better delayed retention.'),gap('r7','ONE WORD: Designers added short ___ to feedback.','explanations','Explanations helped learners understand errors.'),tf('r8','Word counts were treated as a complete measure of essay quality.','FALSE','D explicitly rejects that approach.'),choice('r9','Which element continued to require teacher discussion?',['Argument development','Counting words','Displaying a score'],0,'D identifies argument development and relevance among teacher-led discussions.'),tf('r10','All learners preferred daily streaks.','FALSE','E describes some learners becoming discouraged by missed days.'),tf('r11','The platform charged an annual fee of £100.','NOT GIVEN','No platform fee is stated anywhere in the passage.'),choice('r12','Which statement best summarises the conclusion?',['More questions alone guarantee learning.','Tools work best with meaningful feedback and responsible design.','Teachers should stop assessing essays.'],1,'F says a large bank is useful only when learners understand and use results.')],
