 {title:'Part A · Online study group induction',script:'The online study group starts on the twelfth of November. Meetings are on Wednesdays at seven thirty in the evening, not seven as previously announced. Each meeting lasts fifty minutes. Please upload your writing draft by Monday at six in the evening so your partner has time to read it. Use a document file rather than a photograph. There are four people in each group. During the first meeting, you will discuss learning goals, not take a formal test. Cameras are optional, but a microphone is needed for speaking practice. If your connection fails, write your response in the chat and send an audio recording later. The programme lasts eight weeks and costs forty pounds in total.',questions:[gap('l1','Write the start date (day and month).',['12 November','November 12','twelfth of November','12th November'],'The programme starts on 12 November.'),gap('l2','Write the meeting start time.',['7:30','19:30','7.30','seven thirty'],'7:00 was the earlier announcement; 7:30 is correct.'),gap('l3','ONE NUMBER: Each meeting lasts ___ minutes.','50','The duration is fifty minutes.'),gap('l4','ONE WORD: Upload the writing draft by ___ at 6 pm.','Monday','The Monday deadline gives partners reading time.'),choice('l5','What happens in the first meeting?',['A formal examination','A discussion of learning goals','A camera test'],1,'The first meeting concerns learning goals, not a formal test.'),choice('l6','What is needed for speaking practice?',['A camera','A microphone','A printed photograph'],1,'Cameras are optional; microphones are needed.')]},
 {title:'Part B · Practice versus performance',script:'A common mistake is to judge learning only by how quickly someone finishes an exercise. In our study, adding explanations made each session slower, but improved scores on a test one week later. The immediate task and the delayed test measure different things. We also found that repeated correct answers on one question do not necessarily transfer to a new context. For this reason, revision should include a similar problem with different wording. Open-ended writing needs additional judgement: a long essay can still fail to answer the question. We recommend combining short objective checks with discussion of ideas and examples. Finally, consistency does not have to mean studying every day. A flexible weekly plan can help learners return after interruptions, particularly when progress is linked to completed work rather than a perfect streak.',questions:[choice('l7','What happened after explanations were added?',['Practice became slower but delayed results improved.','Both speed and delayed results declined.','Learners stopped receiving feedback.'],0,'The lecturer distinguishes slower sessions from improved delayed-test performance.'),gap('l8','ONE WORD: The later test occurred one ___ afterwards.','week','The delay is one week.'),choice('l9','Why change wording during revision?',['To test transfer to a new context','To hide every correct answer','To remove relevant vocabulary'],0,'Repeated success on the same question does not guarantee transfer.'),tf('l10','According to the recording, every long essay answers its question effectively.','FALSE','The lecturer explicitly says a long essay may fail to answer the question.'),gap('l11','ONE WORD: Combine objective checks with ___ of ideas and examples.','discussion','Discussion adds judgement to objective checks.'),choice('l12','Which progress measure is recommended?',['An uninterrupted daily streak only','Completed work within a flexible plan','Time spent keeping an app open'],1,'The final sentence recommends completed work rather than a perfect streak.')]}
